## Timing: When to Book or Apply Before Prom

Timing is where most prom nail plans quietly go wrong.

**Acrylics:** Book your appointment two to three days before prom. A fresh set applied close to the event means no visible regrowth and a pristine finish in photos. Book the slot itself at least three weeks ahead, as good nail technicians fill up fast in prom season.

**Gel manicure:** One to two days before is the sweet spot. Gel polish at its freshest has the highest shine. Done four or five days prior, it still looks good, but the initial gloss settles by then.

**Press-ons:** The night before or the morning of prom. Nail glue needs a full cure, so apply at least eight to twelve hours before you need them to perform. The evening before is ideal: fully bonded by morning, no salon rush.

