## Which Is Best for You? A Quick Decision Guide

**Budget shopper:** Press-ons, full stop. A quality set applied with nail glue costs a fraction of a salon appointment and delivers the same visual result for one night.

**Drama-seeker (you want length and impact):** Acrylics if you have the budget and lead time, or Gel-X for similar drama with less chemical exposure. Press-ons in coffin or stiletto shapes are genuinely excellent now too. All lengths and styles work across all three nail types, so <a href='/blog/short-prom-nails'>short nail fans, this post is for you</a> as well.

**First-timer:** Start with gel or press-ons. Acrylic application on unfamiliar nails can be overwhelming: the smell, the filing, the rigid result. Save acrylics for a lower-stakes situation first.

**Short-notice (prom is in two days or less):** Press-ons. No booking required, no drying time, no salon wait. Apply the night before with nail glue.

**Sensitive nails:** Press-ons are the least invasive option. If you want a salon set, gel is a safer starting point than acrylics, particularly with any history of skin reactions to cosmetic products.

